n\nAlso consider opponents\u2019 discards: Next player meld [J1,J1,J1], previous player melds [B2,B2,B2], [B9,B9,B9], [W3,W4,W5].  \nSo Dots B2,B3,B4,B5,B9 have been used a lot. B6 still available=2, B7=3, B8=4. So maybe Dots still possible but my hand leans Bamboo.  \n\nFinal choice: Discard B7 to move towards Bamboo-focused hand, keeps all Bamboo tiles including T2,T5,T6,T7,T8,T9 for maximum sequence/pair options.  \n\nReason:  \nDiscarding B7 reduces suits, keeping flexibility to form Chow sequences in Bamboo suit (T). With T7 and T8 pairs and many T5,T6,T9 singles, I can wait for multiple draws to complete two more melds and a pair. B7 is the only isolated tile in another suit without strong sequence potential given remaining tiles.  \n\nAnswer: Play B7"}
